\newlabel{fig:aggregation-descent}{{3}{19}{Variational free energy \(F(q, a)\) as a function of block-coordinate descent iteration. Source relation: original project objective-descent diagnostic; estimand: free energy in nats by iteration; uncertainty: none for the deterministic seeded run. The trace is a single \protect \breaktt {variational\_aggregate} fusion of a \(7\)-agent contaminated colony (robustness \(1.50\)). x-axis: block-coordinate iteration number; y-axis: \(F(q, a)\) in nats. The curve is monotone non-increasing across all recorded iterations (largest single-step increase: \(8.88 \times 10^{-16}\) nats, at machine precision) and the implementation reports converged status Yes at value \(2.3780\) nats. This verifies objective descent on the executed run --- a diagnostic the \protect \breaktt {robust\_aggregate} heuristic does not provide. Deterministic seeded run; no error band}{fig:aggregation-descent}{}}
\@writefile{snm}{\beamer@slide {fig:aggregation-descent}{19}}
\@writefile{nav}{\headcommand {\slideentry {0}{1}{13}{19/19}{Contamination sweep: regime-dependent server behavior under declared attacks}{0}}}
